DISPOSITION
================================================================================
A complete, HIG-native SwiftUI BackupRestorePage shipped at parity with the web source: a pure
@Observable BackupRestorePageModel (ADR-004 — no networking in the view) exposing loading/empty/
error/success over an injectable BackupRestoreDataSource seam, owning the full create/edit/delete/
trigger/quick-backup/verify/restore-preview interaction + transient toast feedback. The page
reproduces the web chrome (title/subtitle + Quick-Backup/New-Config actions), the error.loadFailed
runs banner, the four headline MetricCards (Total Configs/Backups, Last Backup, Total Size), and
the two GlassPanels — the configurations table (adaptive columnar Grid on macOS/iPad, cards on
iPhone) with per-config Trigger/Edit/Delete, and the run-history table with Download/Verify/Preview
plus the Recent-Errors strip — using P2 tokens + P3 shared components (no hand-rolled glass). The
create/edit, delete-confirm, and restore-preview dialogs are HIG-native sheets with dynamic
provider-credential fields. Every visible string resolves from Localizable.xcstrings with the web
key names (81 keys added: 80 + route.backup; common.cancel pre-existing); byte/int/duration/relative
formatters are ported and harness-tested. The full iOS app BUILD SUCCEEDED; swiftlint --strict,
swiftformat, and the placeholder scan are GREEN; the 30-assertion model harness passed 0-failures.

